    "updated_at": "2021-10-18T10:29:59Z",
    "body": "It seems that the new nix shell sets these environment variables (using `hello` as the perennial test)\r\n\r\n```\r\nANY_NIX_SHELL_PKGS= nixpkgs#hello\r\nIN_NIX_RUN=1\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is on\r\n```\r\n❯ nix-info      \r\nsystem: \"x86_64-linux\", multi-user?: yes, version: nix-env (Nix) 2.5pre20211007_844dd90, nixpkgs: /nix/store/c7mhbzh2kyay2gdaplk87bvnii6aidzm-source\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt also seems to be what  [any-nix-shell](https://github.com/haslersn/any-nix-shell/blob/master/bin/.any-nix-wrapper#L36) utilises \r\n\r\nSide note: would it be possible to port the features of that project into starship?\r\n\r\nDoes this provide a way forward? Happy to take a stab at a pull request ",
